<title>TURKEY: TURKISH BRISA H1 PROFITS RISE.</title>
<headline>TURKISH BRISA H1 PROFITS RISE.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 4,260.65  vs   2,869.72</p>
<p>    Net profit		  4,529.07  vs   3,050.51</p>
<p>    Net sales		  18,836.45  vs  10,867.45</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  6,065.85  vs   3,924.17</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	2,061.30  vs     970.63</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 149.23  vs	27.73</p>
<p>    Total debts		 9,298.22  vs   5,212.01</p>
<p>    Equity		     19,400.98  vs  10,880.31</p>
<p>    Capital		     1,063.13  vs   1,063.13</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish tyre maker Brisa-Bridgestone Sabanci Lastik Sanayi ve Ticaret A.S. is jointly owned by Japan's Bridgestone Corp and Turkish industrial conglomerate Sabanci .</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
